# Family dinners
Never miss a family dinner without telling the dead|They wait|A man misses a family dinner without telling his dead father; his father waits at the table, and the food never goes cold.|MAN; WIFE; FATHER|A dining table with an empty chair|He was busy|The father is waiting for him|The table, the empty chair, the father's plate|invitation|sad
Never move a dead relative's chair|They move you|A man moves his dead father's chair; the chair moves back every night, and the man wakes on the floor.|MAN; WIFE; FATHER|A dining room with a chair|He wanted to rearrange the room|The father is keeping his seat|The chair, the man on the floor, the father's photo|routine|sad
Never serve a family dinner without the extra plate|Someone sits|A mother serves dinner without the extra plate for her dead son; a chair pulls out, and the plate appears, empty.|MOTHER; FATHER; SON|A dining table with four plates|She wanted to move on|The son is sitting at the table|The table, the empty plate, the mother's hand|invitation|sad
Don't argue at a family dinner|The argument continues without you|A family argues at dinner; the argument continues after everyone leaves, and the voices come from the empty chairs.|FAMILY; MOTHER; FATHER|A dining room with empty chairs|They were tired|The argument is living in the room|The chairs, the voices, the cold food|contamination|eerie
Never eat the first bite at a family dinner|The dead eat first|A boy eats the first bite at a family dinner; the food turns cold, and the dead relatives start eating from his plate.|BOY; MOTHER; THE DEAD|A dining table with a full plate|He was hungry|The dead have been waiting for the first bite|The plate, the boy's hand, the empty chairs|invitation|eerie
Don't leave the table before the eldest|The eldest leaves with you|A young man leaves the table before his grandmother; his grandmother leaves with him, and doesn't come back.|MAN; GRANDMOTHER; MOTHER|A dining table with the eldest|He was late|The grandmother is following him|The table, the grandmother's empty chair, the man's car|departure|sad
Never count the family at dinner|The count includes the dead|A woman counts the family at dinner; the count includes her dead sister, who is sitting at the table.|WOMAN; MOTHER; SISTER|A dining table with six chairs|She was setting the table|The sister has been attending every dinner|The table, the sister's chair, the woman's hand|counting|sad
Don't cook a dead relative's favorite dish|They come to eat|A woman cooks her dead husband's favorite dish; he comes to dinner, and asks her to join him.|WOMAN; HUSBAND; DAUGHTER|A kitchen with a favorite dish|She missed him|The husband is taking her with him|The dish, the husband's hand, the woman's plate|invitation|sad
Never lock the dining room after dinner|The family stays|A man locks the dining room after dinner; the family stays inside, and he can't open the door.|MAN; WIFE; FAMILY|A dining room with a locked door|He wanted privacy|The family is still eating|The door, the family, the man's key|threshold|eerie
Don't clear the table alone|Someone helps|A woman clears the table alone after dinner; a hand takes a plate from her, and no one is there.|WOMAN; HUSBAND; THE HAND|A dining room with dirty plates|She was tired|The hand is her dead mother's|The plates, the hand, the woman's face|invitation|sad
